Checks for entry 011 (posts/011-left-0.html).

  cleanup_check.py  the check: does a cleanup command and the count that
                    confirms it share a blind spot?
  mutate.py         11 deliberate breaks of cleanup_check.py
  repro.zsh         the 2026-11-13 commands replayed against ./tmp (a
                    symlink) and ./T, standing in for /tmp and $TMPDIR

Python 3, no packages. Run from this directory (mutate.py reads
cleanup_check.py from here). Tested on macOS only:

  python3 cleanup_check.py "find {root} -maxdepth 1 -name {pat} -exec rmdir {} +" \
      "find {root} -maxdepth 1 -name {pat} | wc -l"
                                                  # expect: FALSE-CLEAN, exit 1
  python3 cleanup_check.py "find {root}/ -maxdepth 1 -name {pat} -exec rmdir {} +" \
      "ls -d {root}/{glob} 2>/dev/null | wc -l"
                                                  # expect: OK, exit 0
  python3 mutate.py                               # expect: 8/11 killed

repro.zsh deletes with rm -rf inside the directory you run it from. Build
the fixture in an empty scratch directory first:

  mkdir private-tmp T && ln -s private-tmp tmp
  for i in $(seq 1 53); do mkdir private-tmp/proj-$i; done
  for i in $(seq 1 42); do mkdir T/proj-$i; done
  zsh /path/to/repro.zsh                          # expect: 42, left= 0, 53
